{
  "dom_id": "step-e21591",
  "name": "Example: Evaluating the Step Function",
  "problem": "Evaluate $f(t) = 9u(t-9)$ at $t=9,$ where $u$ is the unit step function.",
  "worked_solution": "The unit step function $u(t)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,t\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\,t<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(t)$ at $t=9,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(9) & =9u(9-9) \\\\  & =9u(0) \\\\  & =9\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(9)=9.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
